Apple today seeded the second beta of an upcoming iOS 27.2 update to developers for testing purposes, with the update coming a week after Apple released the first iOS 27.2 beta. Apple also seeded an iPadOS 27.2 beta.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065585" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iOS-27.2-Next-to-iPhone.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" /><br/>
Registered developers can download the beta updates by opting in under Settings &gt; General &gt; Software Update and selecting the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> developer beta.<br/>
<br/>
iOS 27.2 includes Apple's redesigned Health app with new Insight and Longevity tabs. It also brings <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI in new languages. There are several other new features, with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ios-27-2-beta-features/">details available in our features guide</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Apple releasing an iOS 27.2 beta ahead of a iOS 27.1 beta was surprise, especially because the company plans to ship the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/iphone-duo-ios-27-1/">iPhone Duo with iOS 27.1</a>. Apple is likely holding iOS 27.1 until the Duo comes out, just to keep the features under wraps. iOS 27.1 will add updated app layouts and features built for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>'s two displays. The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; will have a vertical dock, vertical <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>, new dual-screen app layouts, side-by-side app multitasking, and exclusive Camera app capabilities.<br/>
<br/>
